## **A second look, for a sum**

The method is for a this. A cup is one kind. A sum is another.

*This: two plus two equals four.*

| What came forward | How much it holds |
| :---- | :---- |
| what two is used for, in counting | strong |
| what plus is used for | strong |
| what four is used for | strong |
| other sums that go the same way | some |
| the marks on the page, the ink | none |
| a rumor that “math is only marks” | none |

Two, plus, and four sit together. Other sums sit nearby. The ink does not hold this up. The rumor does not. Those are leftover of this look. “Numbers exist in themselves” stays off leftover. That belongs to the rim.

The list is not the sum. People already added. This is a sum-under-a-look. This look is not the world. Adding in the ordinary way is still allowed. If someone wants 0 through 3, use the same rungs as the cup. No new scale. No average.

## **A rewritten this is a second look**

This is not a closer meaning, and it is not a third specimen.

Write: the sky is blue. Daylight, the word blue, other days the sky looked this way may hold. A football stadium at night may not come forward. If it comes forward and does not hold that this, it is leftover of that look.

Now write it down another way: the sky over the stadium looks blue under the lights. Run the same questions. The stadium lights may now hold. What sat out can move.

*The sky did not change. The box did. That is a second look.*

# **Conclusion**

*The ordinary thing continues*

A look starts in the middle, on something already here. Difference shows up because a this only appears against what is not it. Some of what came forward points back and holds. Some of it came forward and does not. That leftover pile is not a defect in the cup, and it is not a second world hiding in the ceramic. The box has a rim: this look is not the world. The world does not have to be tidy, or a simulation, or turtles all the way down, for that much to be the case.

You can open a support, write it down another way, look at the looking, or stop.

*The drawing can get as dense as it wants. The ordinary thing continues.*

Density is allowed. It is not required, and it is not a better look.

The thick book exists if you want the machinery. This page is not that machinery. Both books go by Expressionalism.

*Looking is optional. Living continues either way.*
